From a91eb11d307a890e24b89a8e658c7ba842e0c219 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 14:44:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] fix(2d): Pass start plans each nested material part from
 its own edges

The third read of PR #3353 (head 9939a6238) found material inside a
hole left standing: the Outside fill read nested outer loops as holes,
so the bore of a hollow boss or the stock inside a ring part got one
ring along its edge and its middle stayed uncut, with no warning.

Each part of the material (an outer loop with its own holes) is now
planned from its own edges; Inside on a part with no hole cuts it core
first, as Auto, with a note. A completeness guard sweeps the passes of
each start-side plan: if more than 0.1 mm2 of the cutter-centre area
stays unswept, the level takes the Auto plan with a named "Pass start"
warning. More clip tests (a vertex on the boundary, a tangent touch, an
edge overlap); non_sliver_center moves to pocket_plan.rs.

Refs #3316

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
