From 3c3f13eb4f8a1d24717b3dce9fb4addd6c38eec9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 17:54:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] fix(2d): the offset pass-start fallback warns

The completeness guard's fallback note ("Pass start <side>: the rings
from the start side would leave A mm2 of this area uncut ...") did not
carry RINGS_FALLBACK, so rings_fallbacks() counted zero and a 2D Offset
posted no StrategyFallback warning when the guard fell back to the Auto
order. Route the note through RINGS_FALLBACK, so the op posts one
advisory Warning::StrategyFallback (#3035) plus the "Pass start" note,
as the rest of the pass-start family does.

Pins: motion linux `the_guard_fallback_is_an_offset_rings_fallback` and
app `the_offset_guard_fallback_is_a_strategy_fallback`; the Inside fig8
pin also asserts that a complete band posts no fallback warning.

Refs #3316

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
